Program 12 — Steps to Execute
Aim

To build and deploy a complete DevOps pipeline using:

GitHub
Maven
Azure DevOps
Self-hosted Agent
Step 1: Create Maven Project

Open CMD and run:

mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=DevOpsFinalLab -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DinteractiveMode=false

Move inside project:

cd DevOpsFinalLab


Check files:

dir

You should see:

pom.xml
src
Step 2: Delete Test Folder

Run:

rmdir /s /q src\test
Step 3: Edit Java File

Open:

src\main\java\com\example\App.java

Replace with:

package com.example;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello from DevOps Final Lab!");
    }
}

Save file.

Step 4: Edit pom.xml

Open pom.xml.

Replace with:

<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0
         http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>DevOpsFinalLab</artifactId>
    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.2.2</version>

                <configuration>
                    <archive>
                        <manifest>
                            <mainClass>com.example.App</mainClass>
                        </manifest>
                    </archive>
                </configuration>

            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>

Save file.

Step 5: Build Maven Project

Run:

mvn clean package

You should see:

BUILD SUCCESS
Step 6: Create Git Repository

Run:

git init
git add .
git commit -m "DevOps Final Lab"
Step 7: Create GitHub Repository

Go to:

GitHub

Create repository:

DevOpsFinalLab
Step 8: Connect GitHub Repo

Run:

git remote remove origin

(ignore error if any)

Then:

git remote add origin https://github.com/Nagashreemurthy21/DevOpsFinalLab.git

Push project:

git branch -M main
git push -u origin main --force
Step 9: Create azure-pipelines.yml

Inside project folder create:

azure-pipelines.yml

Paste:

trigger:
- main

pool:
  name: NagashreeAgent

steps:
- task: Maven@3
  inputs:
    mavenPomFile: 'pom.xml'
    goals: 'clean package'

- script: |
    echo "Simulating deployment..."
    mkdir deployed
    copy target\*.jar deployed\
    echo "Deployment successful!"
  displayName: 'Simulate Deployment'

- script: |
    echo "Running the JAR file..."
    java -jar deployed\*.jar
  displayName: 'Run Application'

Save file.

Step 10: Push YAML File

Run:

git add .
git commit -m "Added Azure pipeline"
git push origin main
Step 11: Start Self-Hosted Agent

Open agent folder CMD.

Run:

.\run.cmd

You should see:

Listening for Jobs
Step 12: Create Azure DevOps Project

Open:

Azure DevOps

Create project:

DevOpsFinalProject
Step 13: Create Pipeline

Go to:

Pipelines
→ Create Pipeline

Choose:

GitHub

Select repository:

DevOpsFinalLab

Choose:

Existing Azure Pipelines YAML file

Select:

azure-pipelines.yml
Step 14: Run Pipeline

Click:

Run Pipeline

Then:

Run
Step 15: Verify Output

Pipeline should become green ✅

Logs should show:

Simulating deployment...
Deployment successful!
Running the JAR file...
Hello from DevOps Final Lab!
Step 16: Verify Deployment Folder

Open:

C:\azureagent\vsts-agent-win-x64-4.273.0\_work\1\s\deployed

You should see .jar file.

Result

Successfully built and deployed a complete DevOps pipeline using Azure DevOps, Maven, GitHub, and self-hosted agent.
